From ad89cd9d072a252d197e9174c7e53e7945d30083 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ayoub Nabil Boubagrat <237098474+ayoubnabil@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 9 Sep 2026 21:50:01 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] avcodec/tiff: clear the separated intermediate buffer

Strip decoding errors are tolerated unless AV_EF_EXPLODE is set. The
separated-to-RGBA conversion still consumes the full intermediate buffer,
including lines that the failed strip did not initialize.

Allocate the buffer with av_calloc() so undecoded lines cannot expose heap
contents in the output frame.

Fixes: read of uninitialized memory
Fixes: 6nbtoGQYPUjZ
Found-by: Ayoub Nabil Boubagrat <237098474+ayoubnabil@users.noreply.github.com>

Use of uninitialized memory Replicated through UnModified FFmpeg with Valgrind
Signed-off-by: Michael Niedermayer <michael@niedermayer.cc>
(cherry picked from commit ad89cd9d072a252d197e9174c7e53e7945d30083)
---
 libavcodec/tiff.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/libavcodec/tiff.c b/libavcodec/tiff.c
index 41db29d6e24..efe7ae7056a 100644
--- a/libavcodec/tiff.c
+++ b/libavcodec/tiff.c
@@ -2216,7 +2216,7 @@ again:
             s->avctx->pix_fmt == AV_PIX_FMT_RGBA) {
             stride = stride * 5 / 4;
             five_planes =
-            dst = av_malloc(stride * s->height);
+            dst = av_calloc(s->height, stride);
             if (!dst)
                 return AVERROR(ENOMEM);
         }
-- 
